cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Empirical error scaling of the Kirchhoff approximation on periodic surfaces with small-scale roughness"
abstract: >-
  Python code and cached data behind the figure, the tables and the numbers of the paper, and the validation scripts. The paper measures,
  against an independent C-method reference with energy conservation as a check, how the error of the Kirchhoff approximation (KA, an
  expansion in the curvature of the surface) depends on its validity parameter C and on the slope s of the small scale, for
  one-dimensional lossless dielectric surfaces made of a smooth periodic profile carrying a small-scale roughness (TE and TM): an
  empirical scaling in (C, s), tolerance limits, and the energy balance as an indicator. It compares KA with the first-order small-slope
  approximation (SSA-1), and uses a boundary-variation series (the method of variation of boundaries taken about the periodic surface,
  with the Kirchhoff amplitudes or the exact solution of the smooth profile as zeroth order) to show what KA misses.
